// A rule which can match the empty string never produces an empty token. MAYBE accepts in the start state, so every
// attempt starts out accepting, but an attempt which consumes nothing leaves the match empty and lands in the error
// path instead. The space in the input is what triggers that, because MAYBE matches nothing there and no other rule
// matches either.
//
// There is deliberately no rule for whitespace, so that the empty match is the only thing which can happen at the
// space.
//
// The parser is not what this case is about, so the grammar is the single empty production the file format requires.

@scanner {
    MAYBE: /a*/;
    B:     "b";
}

@parser {
    tokens
        : @empty
        ;
}
